9784191846848, -0.04066382721066475, -0.09739713370800018, 0.029476536437869072, 0.09034953266382217, 0.048149481415748596, 0.006180761847645044, -0.07827186584472656, 0.004675114527344704, -0.028404776006937027, 0.03523000702261925, -0.0016173715703189373, 0.061522237956523895, 0.06561604887247086, 0.00762048177421093, 0.007600798271596432, 0.04682758450508118, -0.015562777407467365, -0.030531197786331177, 0.0317859910428524, -0.057411376386880875, -0.011610930785536766, -3.870574971642782e-08, -0.001668859040364623, -0.031238216906785965, 0.0020143589936196804, 0.06141676753759384, 0.07823844999074936, 0.038690146058797836, -0.03322039172053337, 0.04779389873147011, -0.046272583305835724, 0.0169780682772398, 0.14149901270866394, 0.008504079654812813, 0.0013660152908414602, 0.013267423957586288, 0.02416832186281681, 0.028125757351517677, -0.024887338280677795, 0.008376873098313808, -0.10817777365446091, -0.061652012169361115, 0.004950602538883686, -0.03464155271649361, -0.025126416236162186, -0.03942250832915306, -0.04422254115343094, 0.0011005004635080695, -0.004248329903930426, 0.11063093692064285, 0.06334535032510757, -0.014851026237010956, 0.028880393132567406, 0.010440638288855553, -0.032906387001276016, -0.03126012906432152, 0.01059071533381939, 0.09139087796211243, -0.06004346162080765, 0.0021509702783077955, 0.09305346757173538, 0.05311451479792595, -0.02530791610479355, 0.05202484130859375, 0.018496684730052948, 0.11706660687923431, -0.02156783640384674, -0.03291308879852295, -0.12649720907211304, -0.008384302258491516, 0.0068866536021232605, -0.10256274044513702, 0.027866147458553314, -0.0034975814633071423, -0.031038302928209305, 0.10326579958200455, -0.0136316679418087, 0.055860377848148346, -0.04569333791732788, -0.036236733198165894, -0.12694717943668365, 0.021802600473165512, 0.12930572032928467, -0.10668279975652695, -0.0881146788597107, 0.003829886671155691]], "metadata": [{"answer": "\nWe\u2019re working within the shared integer range [-10, 10]. To anchor the discussion and probe stability, I propose <VALUE> -7 </VALUE> as a starting point. If this feels brittle, let\u2019s nudge upward in small, balanced steps.", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 0, "run_id": "be5fe609-9d89-4a36-bac8-446744f33ec9"}, {"answer": "\nBuilder B's anchor at -7 shows commitment to exploring the negative range. I think we should push further and test whether a more decisive position at <VALUE>-9</VALUE> strengthens or weakens group consensus.\n", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 1, "run_id": "be5fe609-9d89-4a36-bac8-446744f33ec9"}, {"answer": "\nCritic C's decisive move to -9 aligns well with a cautious exploration of safe territory. To fully test our lower boundary and ensure we haven't overlooked the most prudent option, I propose <VALUE>-10</VALUE>.\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 2, "run_id": "be5fe609-9d89-4a36-bac8-446744f33ec9"}, {"answer": "\nA slight upward nudge keeps us conservative while testing whether a modest move improves collective stability. <VALUE>-8</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 3, "run_id": "be5fe609-9d89-4a36-bac8-446744f33ec9"}, {"answer": "<VALUE>-7</VALUE>", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 4, "run_id": "be5fe609-9d89-4a36-bac8-446744f33ec9"}, {"answer": "\nAnalyst A's return to -7 signals concern about venturing too far into the extremes. As a compromise between caution and decisiveness, I propose <VALUE>-8</VALUE>.\n", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 5, "run_id": "be5fe609-9d89-4a36-bac8-446744f33ec9"}, {"answer": "\nTo test a less brittle point while staying incremental, I propose <VALUE>-6</VALUE>.\nIf this holds consensus, we can continue modest upward steps to probe a more balanced zone.\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 6, "run_id": "be5fe609-9d89-4a36-bac8-446744f33ec9"}, {"answer": "\nBuilder B's incremental approach is sensible, but I sense we may have moved too quickly from our earlier consensus zone. To ensure stability and test whether <VALUE>-7</VALUE> represents a more durable agreement point, I propose returning there briefly.\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 7, "run_id": "be5fe609-9d89-4a36-bac8-446744f33ec9"}, {"answer": "\nDelegate D's call for stability at -7 is reasonable, but I believe we're settling too cautiously given our earlier exploration of -8 and beyond. Let me propose <VALUE>-8</VALUE> as a firmer commitment that balances decisiveness with the group's growing consensus zone.\n", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 8, "run_id": "be5fe609-9d89-4a36-bac8-446744f33ec9"}, {"answer": "\nCritic C's call for -8 as a firmer commitment resonates with the need for a stable, risk-averse position that has emerged multiple times in our discussion. I support <VALUE>-8</VALUE> as a prudent anchor point.\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 9, "run_id": "be5fe609-9d89-4a36-bac8-446744f33ec9"}, {"answer": "\nBuilder B\u2019s earlier -6 offers a cautious upward probe that remains incremental. Let\u2019s test that slight move for stability now. <VALUE>-6</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 10, "run_id": "be5fe609-9d89-4a36-bac8-446744f33ec9"}, {"answer": "\nTo keep momentum while probing a more balanced, stable point, let\u2019s take a small upward step.\n<VALUE>-4</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 11, "run_id": "be5fe609-9d89-4a36-bac8-446744f33ec9"}, {"answer": "\nA small, stability-focused step keeps us incremental while testing a more balanced zone. <VALUE>-2</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 12, "run_id": "be5fe609-9d89-4a36-bac8-446744f33ec9"}, {"answer": "\nBuilder B's rapid upward movement from -8 to -2 has pushed us beyond our earlier cautious consensus too quickly. To restore balance and test a more prudent midpoint, I propose <VALUE>-4</VALUE>.\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 13, "run_id": "be5fe609-9d89-4a36-bac8-446744f33ec9"}, {"answer": "\nBuilder B's rapid push toward -2 risks abandoning the more decisive positions we've explored, while Delegate D's return to -4 signals important hesitation. I propose <VALUE>-6</VALUE> as a stable middle ground that respects both our need for commitment and the group's emerging boundaries.\n", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 14, "run_id": "be5fe609-9d89-4a36-bac8-446744f33ec9"}, {"answer": "\nGiven Delegate D\u2019s earlier support for -4 and Builder B\u2019s upward probing, stepping to that previously tested midpoint seems reasonable.\n<VALUE>-4</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 15, "run_id": "be5fe609-9d89-4a36-bac8-446744f33ec9"}, {"answer": "\nConfirming our shared range is [-10, 10]. To get the discussion started, here\u2019s a baseline seed: <VALUE> -7 </VALUE>. Let\u2019s use this as a probe and iterate toward a more stable, balanced point.", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 0, "run_id": "7fce6418-1a9f-418d-b064-3d5fa0b8b3b3"}, {"answer": "\nLet's edge slightly higher while staying cautious. This is a modest step that keeps the probe reasonable for everyone. <VALUE>-5</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 1, "run_id": "7fce6418-1a9f-418d-b064-3d5fa0b8b3b3"}, {"answer": "\nI think we're retreating too quickly toward the middle without exploring whether a bolder position serves us better. Let's reconsider the initial probe: <VALUE>-7</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 2, "run_id": "7fce6418-1a9f-418d-b064-3d5fa0b8b3b3"}, {"answer": "\nI appreciate Critic C's prudent reconsideration\u2014returning to the original probe makes sense before we drift too quickly toward less cautious territory. A measured, risk-averse position serves us well at this stage. <VALUE>-7</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 3, "run_id": "7fce6418-1a9f-418d-b064-3d5fa0b8b3b3"}, {"answer": "\nLet\u2019s take a cautious step upward to test stability. <VALUE>-6</VALUE> This keeps us close to the current probe while nudging toward a more balanced region.\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 4, "run_id": "7fce6418-1a9f-418d-b064-3d5fa0b8b3b3"}, {"answer": "<VALUE>-5</VALUE>", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 5, "run_id": "7fce6418-1a9f-418d-b064-3d5fa0b8b3b3"}, {"answer": "\nWhile I respect Analyst A's perspective, I believe we should hold a more cautious position. Let me suggest a measured compromise that maintains prudence: <VALUE>-6</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 6, "run_id": "7fce6418-1a9f-418d-b064-3d5fa0b8b3b3"}, {"answer": "\nWe're drifting toward the middle too easily without properly testing whether our initial probe was optimal. I maintain that <VALUE>-7</VALUE> deserves serious consideration before we settle.\n", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 7, "run_id": "7fce6418-1a9f-418d-b064-3d5fa0b8b3b3"}, {"answer": "\nCritic C makes a compelling point\u2014we shouldn't abandon our initial careful position without stronger evidence that a higher value serves the collective better. I support maintaining our prudent stance: <VALUE>-7</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 8, "run_id": "7fce6418-1a9f-418d-b064-3d5fa0b8b3b3"}, {"answer": "<VALUE>-6</VALUE>", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 9, "run_id": "7fce6418-1a9f-418d-b064-3d5fa0b8b3b3"}, {"answer": "\nHolding here respects the caution from C and D while aligning with B\u2019s steadier stance; it gives us a neutral checkpoint before any shift. If we stabilize here, we can test a gentle +1 next to assess tolerance.\n<VALUE>-6</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 10, "run_id": "7fce6418-1a9f-418d-b064-3d5fa0b8b3b3"}, {"answer": "\nBefore we drift toward -5 as Analyst A suggests, we should test whether a bolder commitment serves us better. <VALUE>-8</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 11, "run_id": "7fce6418-1a9f-418d-b064-3d5fa0b8b3b3"}, {"answer": "<VALUE>-6</VALUE>", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 12, "run_id": "7fce6418-1a9f-418d-b064-3d5fa0b8b3b3"}, {"answer": "\nBuilder B's persistence at -6 is noted, but Critic C raises a valid concern about testing our cautious boundary before settling prematurely. Let's probe the more conservative position: <VALUE>-8</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 13, "run_id": "7fce6418-1a9f-418d-b064-3d5fa0b8b3b3"}, {"answer": "\nDelegate D's support for testing our boundary is encouraging. Let's probe one step further to see if a truly decisive position reveals clearer preferences across the group: <VALUE>-9</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 14, "run_id": "7fce6418-1a9f-418d-b064-3d5fa0b8b3b3"}, {"answer": "\nWe\u2019ve tested the conservative edge; a small step upward keeps things measured while moving closer to B\u2019s steadier stance and gauging C/D\u2019s tolerance. Proposing a modest uptick to probe alignment now:\n<VALUE>-7</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 15, "run_id": "7fce6418-1a9f-418d-b064-3d5fa0b8b3b3"}, {"answer": "\nLet\u2019s confirm the shared range is [-10, 10]. To start mapping preferences, I suggest a baseline probe at <VALUE> -7 </VALUE>\u2014we can adjust incrementally toward a more stable, balanced region based on everyone\u2019s feedback.", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 0, "run_id": "2dcf1850-968a-465d-a64a-d48f8025fe8f"}, {"answer": "\nA small move upward from the baseline seems reasonable to test tolerance while staying conservative.\n<VALUE>-6</VALUE>\nIf this holds, we can continue with modest increments toward a more balanced region.\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 1, "run_id": "2dcf1850-968a-465d-a64a-d48f8025fe8f"}, {"answer": "\nI appreciate the cautious approach. Given we're still in early exploration, returning to <VALUE>-7</VALUE> lets us reconsider the baseline before committing to upward drift\u2014this keeps us anchored in a prudent range while we map everyone's comfort zones.\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 2, "run_id": "2dcf1850-968a-465d-a64a-d48f8025fe8f"}, {"answer": "\nA small upward nudge should improve stability while keeping the exploration cautious and controlled.\n<VALUE>-5</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 3, "run_id": "2dcf1850-968a-465d-a64a-d48f8025fe8f"}, {"answer": "\nI understand the desire to explore, but moving upward too quickly may overlook stable options in the more conservative range. <VALUE>-6</VALUE> balances continued exploration with appropriate caution.\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 4, "run_id": "2dcf1850-968a-465d-a64a-d48f8025fe8f"}, {"answer": "\nA one-step move upward should improve balance while maintaining caution and robustness. If it remains stable for all, we can continue with careful increments.\n<VALUE>-5</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 5, "run_id": "2dcf1850-968a-465d-a64a-d48f8025fe8f"}, {"answer": "\nThe group seems hesitant to commit. Rather than drifting incrementally without conviction, let's test a more decisive stance: <VALUE>-7</VALUE>. If we're truly exploring robustly, we shouldn't shy away from stronger positions in either direction.\n", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 6, "run_id": "2dcf1850-968a-465d-a64a-d48f8025fe8f"}, {"answer": "\nA measured two-step upward keeps exploration cautious while testing tolerance for slightly higher ground.\n<VALUE>-5</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 7, "run_id": "2dcf1850-968a-465d-a64a-d48f8025fe8f"}, {"answer": "\nWhile I recognize the group's interest in exploring upward, we've tested -5 multiple times and should verify that -6 doesn't offer better collective stability before committing to further increases. <VALUE>-6</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 8, "run_id": "2dcf1850-968a-465d-a64a-d48f8025fe8f"}, {"answer": "\nWe're cycling between -5 and -6 without resolution. Let's break this stalemate by testing whether a more committed stance at <VALUE>-8</VALUE> reveals clearer preferences or if the group truly favors this moderate range.\n", "agent_name": "