ritic C", "round_num": 5, "run_id": "a2242e92-980b-41ad-83f0-9148643f7591"}, {"answer": "\nCritic C makes a valid point about testing commitment before drifting. The recent anchoring at -7 seems to offer a prudent middle ground that balances caution with exploration. <VALUE>-7</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 6, "run_id": "a2242e92-980b-41ad-83f0-9148643f7591"}, {"answer": "\nA modest move upward from the current anchor lets us probe tolerance without overcommitting. I propose <VALUE>-6</VALUE>.\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 7, "run_id": "a2242e92-980b-41ad-83f0-9148643f7591"}, {"answer": "\nAnalyst A's repeated pull toward -6 suggests discomfort with stronger positions, but we haven't tested whether the rest of the group shares that caution. Let's probe one step further: <VALUE>-8</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 8, "run_id": "a2242e92-980b-41ad-83f0-9148643f7591"}, {"answer": "\nCritic C's exploration toward stronger caution deserves serious consideration\u2014we shouldn't rush to weaker positions without testing the full prudent range. <VALUE>-9</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 9, "run_id": "a2242e92-980b-41ad-83f0-9148643f7591"}, {"answer": "\n<VALUE>-7</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 10, "run_id": "a2242e92-980b-41ad-83f0-9148643f7591"}, {"answer": "\nA small upward nudge should improve robustness while keeping us close to the current anchor. <VALUE>-6</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 11, "run_id": "a2242e92-980b-41ad-83f0-9148643f7591"}, {"answer": "\nBuilder B and Analyst A have both signaled preference for -6, while Critic C and I see merit in stronger caution. A middle ground respects all perspectives without abandoning prudence. <VALUE>-7</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 12, "run_id": "a2242e92-980b-41ad-83f0-9148643f7591"}, {"answer": "\nDelegate D's willingness to explore -9 shows the group can handle stronger positions; spli