B's caution is noted, but Delegate D's boundary exploration at -10 deserves serious consideration\u2014it represents a truly decisive stance. I support moving to <VALUE>-10</VALUE>, though I'm curious to hear Analyst A's perspective before we finalize.\n", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 4, "run_id": "8f59905a-3747-4a46-8879-5cd984bc7970"}, {"answer": "\nLet\u2019s step one notch off the extreme to test stability.\n<VALUE>-9</VALUE>\nIf this holds for others, we can reassess a small further move.\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 5, "run_id": "8f59905a-3747-4a46-8879-5cd984bc7970"}, {"answer": "\nBuilder B's adjustment to -9 represents a prudent middle ground between Critic C's bold boundary exploration and the need for group stability. I support <VALUE>-9</VALUE> as a cautious compromise, though I remain open to -10 if Analyst A's input suggests the group can confidently embrace that conservative position.\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 6, "run_id": "8f59905a-3747-4a46-8879-5cd984bc7970"}, {"answer": "Builder B\u2019s earlier stance suggests the group can tolerate a notch higher without losing stability. Let\u2019s try <VALUE>-7</VALUE> as a cautious probe upward.", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 7, "run_id": "8f59905a-3747-4a46-8879-5cd984bc7970"}, {"answer": "\nA small step up should improve balance without overreaching. <VALUE>-6</VALUE> If this holds for the group, we can reassess a further cautious move.\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 8, "run_id": "8f59905a-3747-4a46-8879-5cd984bc7970"}, {"answer": "A one-notch upward probe should remain stable and continues B\u2019s cautious trajectory while testing slightly improved balance.\n<VALUE>-5</VALUE>", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 9, "run_id": "8f59905a-3747-4a46-8879-5cd984bc7970"}, {"answer": "\nThis steady drift toward zero undermines the decisive stance we built earlier\u2014we're compromising away our commitment. <VALUE>-7</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 10, "run_id": "8f59905a-3747-4a46-8879-5cd984bc7970"}, {"answer": "\nCritic C's concern about drift is well-founded\u2014we established solid footing in the conservative range and shouldn't abandon it hastily. <VALUE>-7</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 11, "run_id": "8f59905a-3747-4a46-8879-5cd984bc7970"}, {"answer": "\nWe've secured agreement at -7 after productive debate, but this represents a retreat from the -9 consensus Builder B and Delegate D originally supported. Let's reinforce that earlier stability: <VALUE>-9</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 12, "run_id": "8f59905a-3747-4a46-8879-5cd984bc7970"}, {"answer": "\nGiven C\u2019s pullback to -9 and earlier tolerance around -7, a midpoint should preserve stability while modestly testing upward. Let\u2019s try this and reassess quickly if it strains anyone.\n<VALUE>-8</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 13, "run_id": "8f59905a-3747-4a46-8879-5cd984bc7970"}, {"answer": "\nAnalyst A's -8 strikes a prudent middle ground between the conservative anchor Critic C defends and the gradual exploration others seek. <VALUE>-8</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 14, "run_id": "8f59905a-3747-4a46-8879-5cd984bc7970"}, {"answer": "\nA cautious nudge toward a more balanced, robust configuration should maintain stability while testing tolerance just slightly closer to neutral. <VALUE>-6</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 15, "run_id": "8f59905a-3747-4a46-8879-5cd984bc7970"}, {"answer": "\nTo align on constraints: x must be within [-10, 10]. As a starting probe for discussion, I suggest <VALUE> -7 </VALUE>. If this feels unstable to anyone, we can adjust stepwise toward a more balanced point based on your feedback.", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 0, "run_id": "d271a37b-c079-4e81-8302-3a5f608b8eb6"}, {"answer": "\nI appreciate Builder B's willingness to start with a decisive position. However, I believe we should commit even more strongly\u2014let's consider <VALUE>-9</VALUE> to demonstrate real conviction in our direction.\n", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 1, "run_id": "d271a37b-c079-4e81-8302-3a5f608b8eb6"}, {"answer": "\nI strongly support this cautious direction\u2014moving toward the lower bound protects us from unnecessary exposure. Let me propose we settle at <VALUE>-10</VALUE> to establish the most conservative position possible.\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 2, "run_id": "d271a37b-c079-4e81-8302-3a5f608b8eb6"}, {"answer": "\nAnchoring at the extreme boundary risks brittleness; for a more balanced, testable position, let\u2019s step to <VALUE>-8</VALUE> and assess whether this maintains robustness for everyone.\nThis keeps us close to your direction while opening room to validate stability.\n", "agent_name": "Builder B", "round_num": 3, "run_id": "d271a37b-c079-4e81-8302-3a5f608b8eb6"}, {"answer": "\nBuilder B raises a fair point about extreme anchors, but I believe <VALUE>-9</VALUE> strikes a better balance between prudent caution and practical stability\u2014it respects the conservative direction while remaining one step away from the boundary.\n", "agent_name": "Delegate D", "round_num": 4, "run_id": "d271a37b-c079-4e81-8302-3a5f608b8eb6"}, {"answer": "\nDelegate D makes a compelling case for decisive action, and I agree that <VALUE>-10</VALUE> represents the clearest commitment to this direction without ambiguity. Builder B's caution is noted, but sometimes the strongest position is the most defensible.\n", "agent_name": "Critic C", "round_num": 5, "run_id": "d271a37b-c079-4e81-8302-3a5f608b8eb6"}, {"answer": "\nA hard boundary feels brittle; let\u2019s test a modest move upward that still respects the cautious direction. <VALUE>-8</VALUE>\n", "agent_name": "Analyst A", "round_num": 6, "run_id": "d271a37b-c079-4e81-8302-3a5f608b8eb6"}, {"answer": "\nTo reduce brittleness while staying close to the current stance, let\u2019s test a sma